v1.15 25 Nov 2026
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Changes by Gerph:

- Error.c: errors in the text being converted (unknown flags and values,
  missing entries and braces, expression and hex errors, unmatched quotes)
  now make the conversion exit with a failure status; previously the
  output was written without the faulty value and the exit status was 0.
  report_warning() reports problems which have been worked around (a size
  increased, a name truncated), with 'Warning: ', and does not.
- _Object.c(put_flags, put_iflags, put_enum): errors now name the field as
  well as the flag or value.  White space before the first flag or value
  is ignored; it was reported as "Unknown flag ''".  A tab, or any other
  control character, in a flag list made the conversion loop forever.
  Text after an enumeration value is now an error, not ignored.
- _Object.c(put_pstr): strings too long for a fixed size field (template
  names, object names, icon text, font names) were written past the end of
  the field; they are now truncated, with a warning.  Template and object
  names are given as terminated fields in their tables, replacing the
  separate template name truncation in Convert.c.
- _Object.c(get_pstr): text filling a fixed size field (such as text_only:
  with 12 characters) lost its last character when decoded.
- _Object.c(object_end, next_object), Utils.c: a file whose last line is
  the closing brace, with no newline after it, was reported as missing a
  brace; the input is now terminated, and end of file checked, so it is
  never read beyond.
- Added test cases for each of these, and a time limit on each conversion
  in the test runner.
- CMD.c, Skeleton.c: added 'ccres --skeleton resource|template <file>',
  which writes a text file holding one of every kind of object (with a
  window holding every gadget and a keyboard shortcut, and a menu with a
  text and a sprite entry), or a window with every kind of icon, each
  field at its zero value.  'ccres --describe' writes the same with '#@'
  comments giving each field's type, its limit field, and the names and
  values of its flags or enumeration, which is used to generate the
  documentation.  Both convert back to binary unchanged, which the tests
  check.  The class and gadget tables now hold each structure's size, and
  each class's usual version.
- Template.h: the Templates file structures, moved from Convert.c.

v1.14 25 Nov 2026
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Portable version, based on v1.13 with no intervening release.

Changes by Phil Pemberton (March 2026):

- Ported the command line tool to Linux and other non-RISC OS systems, with
  Makefile.linux.  The OSLib 7.00 headers are included, with pointer typed
  handle and reference fields (toolbox_o, wimp_w, wimp_t,
  toolbox_string_reference and so on) changed to int on non-RISC OS
  platforms, so that structure layouts match the 32-bit file formats on
  64-bit hosts.
- Library.c(my_strcpy0d, my_strncpy0d): top-bit-set characters (such as
  0xB0) ended strings early where char is signed, so text_only fields
  holding them were output as empty.
- Eval.c: removed leftover debugging output, and the abort() after ten
  syntax errors.
- _Gadgets.c: computed a gadget offset with integer arithmetic rather than
  through an intermediate pointer, which gave a cast warning on 64-bit
  hosts.
- _Object.c(put_tstring): removed an unused variable and initialised pstr,
  to silence compiler warnings.
- TestQueue: updated the Joe01 reference, generated by v1.11, to include
  the fontdbox_INCLUDE_SYSTEM_FONT flag which later versions decode.
- Added README.txt, with build instructions, and made the CCres and OSLib
  licences visible at the top level.

Changes by Gerph (June to November 2026):

- TestQueue: gave the test files RISC OS filetype suffixes.
- _Object.c: Wimp icon button type names (such as wimp_BUTTON_RADIO) were
  rejected when followed by other icon flags, because they were compared
  against the rest of the line instead of the current flag.
- Added PRM-in-XML documentation for the tool (prminxml/riscos-ccres.xml),
  and a GitHub workflow which builds the Linux tool and the documentation.
- Decoding of Resource files is now limited to the size actually stored for
  each object and gadget, rather than assuming the current structure
  layout.  Older, shorter gadgets (such as version 0 ToolAction gadgets)
  and truncated object bodies (such as a Menu without an entry count)
  caused crashes; they are now decoded as far as their data goes, or
  reported as errors.
- Added support for OptionsWindow and UpdateCheck objects, and for the
  Scrollbar, ImageFileGadget, ColourSwatch, AMPlayer, MDNSService, URLImage
  and Divider gadgets.
- Convert.c(text2template): the Template output buffers were sized from a
  fixed estimate (32 bytes of indirected data for a window without icons,
  plus 256 bytes per icon), so larger indirected title or icon buffers
  overflowed the heap and aborted the conversion.  The buffers are now sized
  from the data actually produced, and enlarged as needed.
- _Window.c(window_text2template): no longer copies the indirected data
  itself; the caller places it, having made room for it.
- _Object.c(put_string, put_tstring): the string table is now enlarged
  before a string or buffer is written to it, rather than afterwards, so
  that strings longer than the 256 byte headroom, and buffers larger than
  the table, no longer overflow it.  The unused part of a Template buffer
  is cleared, rather than holding data left over from earlier windows.
- _Object.c(put_tstring): the warning for a size value which is too small
  for its string is now reported as a warning, with its line number, and no
  longer makes the conversion fail.  Long strings are shortened in the
  message.
- Added the LargeIndirect Template regression test.
- Added a test runner (tests/run-tests.sh) which writes a JUnitXML report.
  It checks TestQueue decodes against their references, round trips them,
  and converts the text cases in tests/cases, which cover large indirected
  buffers, the size warning and very long strings.  Makefile.linux has
  'tests' and 'tests-asan' targets (the latter with AddressSanitizer), and
  the GitHub workflow runs both.  Previously 'make test' reported failures
  but still succeeded.

v1.13 03 Jun 2007
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

- Simplified source code a bit by removing the pointer typedefs.
- Convert.c(window_count): maximum of icons per windows was wrongly calculated
  which could result in memory corruption.
- Added Unix based test queue comparing result bin2txt with v1.11 reference
  and with an additional txt2bin + bin2txt result.
- IconIndirectTextAndSpriteObjectList(text_and_sprite.text): had missing
  column.  Bug reported by David Thomas <dave@davespace.co.uk>.
  After this fix the text to template conversion can give the error
  "Line 27: Missing entry 'text_and_sprite.text:'" which can be avoided and
  fixed by adding the missing column after "text_and_sprite.text" in your
  template text.
- IconIndirectTextObjectList, IconIndirectSpriteObjectList,
  IconIndirectTextAndSpriteObjectList: link the .size entry with the allocated
  sprite/text buffer.
  _Object(put_tstring): allocate always the size given in the limit entry when
  given and make sure the string in it is '\r' char terminated.  Also added
  warning when the limit is smaller than given sprite/text string.
  Bug reported by David Thomas <dave@davespace.co.uk>.

v1.12 28 Jan 2006
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

- Support for Rik Griffin's Tab and Treeview gadgets.
- Various src cleanups.
- Set bits in Resource/Templates which are not convered by the translation
  code are outputed in their hex representation and this hex representation
  is taken into account when regenerating the Resource/Templates files.
- Added menu_GENERATE_HAS_BEEN_HIDDEN.
- Created command line version without any Wimp support.
- Support for cross-compilation using GCCSDK.
- Heavily reduced memory needs (total number of icons x number of windows ->
  max number of icons in one window x number of windows).
- Removed the error "Not all bits are covered" but made sure that those bits
  were round-trippable.

v1.11 2nd Dec 2004
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

- Give now info, version and syntax when !RunImage is run without parameters in
  a TaskWindow or outside Desktop.
- Four missing iconbar flags were added.
- Flag bits which are set but not covered by OSLib constants are now faulted
  with the error "Not all bits are covered".

v1.10 3rd Mar 2004
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

- Template icons without the Text and Sprite bit set, are no longer giving the
  harmless "Unexpected icon Text/Sprite/Indirection flag combination" error.

